API-15: rescale a gage's rainfall when its scale factor is changed during a run

convertRainfall() applies the scale factor when a record is read, so the
current rainfall and the read-ahead rainfall of the next record keep the old
factor after swmm_setValue(swmm_GAGE_SCALEFACTOR), and a co-gage, which
divides that rainfall by the primary gage's new factor, gets a wrong value
until both records have passed. Multiply both by new/old factor in the two
setters (swmm_setValue and swmm_setValueExpanded), so the new factor applies
from the next runoff step.

Apply from the root of a Stormwater-Management-Model checkout at cb3e192b:
    git apply API-15_swmm530.patch

diff --git a/src/legacy/engine/swmm5.c b/src/legacy/engine/swmm5.c
index 4096c9a..9b61d91 100644
--- a/src/legacy/engine/swmm5.c
+++ b/src/legacy/engine/swmm5.c
@@ -1403,7 +1403,13 @@ int EXPORT_OPENSWMMCORE_SOLVER_API swmm_setValue(int property, int index, double
         if (index < 0 || index >= Nobjects[GAGE])
             return 0;
         if (value > 0.0)
+        {
+            // --- rescale the current and read-ahead rainfall, which were
+            //     converted with the old factor
+            Gage[index].rainfall *= value / Gage[index].scaleFactor;
+            Gage[index].nextRainfall *= value / Gage[index].scaleFactor;
             Gage[index].scaleFactor = value;
+        }
         return 0;
     case swmm_SUBCATCH_RPTFLAG:
         if (!IsStartedFlag && index >= 0 && index < Nobjects[SUBCATCH])
@@ -1999,6 +2005,10 @@ int setGageValue(int property, int index, int subIndex, double value)
     case swmm_GAGE_SCALEFACTOR:
         if (value > 0.0)
         {
+            // --- rescale the current and read-ahead rainfall, which were
+            //     converted with the old factor
+            Gage[index].rainfall *= value / Gage[index].scaleFactor;
+            Gage[index].nextRainfall *= value / Gage[index].scaleFactor;
             Gage[index].scaleFactor = value;
             return 0;
         }
